All four routes remain fully open in both directions:  
- c1–g5 traverses the empty d2-e3-f4 diagonal (e2 knight does not intersect it);  
- f1–g2 is a single adjacent diagonal step (g4 pawn does not obstruct);  
- b8–d7 is a standard knight leap with b8 empty in Position 2;  
- f8–e7 is a single adjacent diagonal step with f8 empty in Position 2.  

No capture, pawn advance, or king/rook displacement is required to execute or reverse these moves, so either chronological order is reachable in a legal game.

